   {
    "id": 1,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "SPY",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Core index position (~35%). Benchmark is SPY, so a large core keeps tracking error low while the stock picks do the work. Backdrop 11-13: fear & greed 30 (Fear), S&P 1M -3.1%, 10y 5.15%, VIX 19.3; 7 of 11 sectors above their 50d. Buying a pullback, not a breakout. Sell/trim if the S&P closes below its 200-day with breadth deteriorating, or to fund a better idea.",
    "review_on": "2026-12-14",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.231841+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.231846+00:00"
   },
   {
    "id": 2,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "ADBE",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Value on a quality franchise: P/E ttm 13.6 (0th percentile of its own 5y range in Argus), forward ~9, FCF margin ~41%, revenue +12-13% YoY every quarter for four quarters, op margin ~35%, consensus FY EPS flat-to-up over 90 days. Market prices AI disruption; numbers don't show it yet. Earnings 12-09 amc. Exit if revenue growth drops under 9% or op margin under 30% on the 12-09 report, or price < 215 (below the 52w support area ~190-215 trend).",
    "review_on": "2026-12-10",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.249636+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.249640+00:00"
   },
   {
    "id": 3,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "META",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Sold-off mega-cap growth: -15.8% 1M after Q3, P/E ttm 21.9 (30th percentile of its history), forward ~18, revenue +26% YoY. Risk I accept: Q3 operating margin fell to 20% (Q1 41%, Q2 31%) on AI spending, FY EPS consensus down 31.8 -> 29.1 in 90 days, short interest doubled, $25B new debt. Sized smaller (10%) for that. Exit if next report (01-26) shows revenue growth < 20% or op margin still falling, or price < 560.",
    "review_on": "2027-01-27",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.267178+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.267182+00:00"
   },
   {
    "id": 4,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "LNG",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Energy diversifier with momentum: LNG exporter, revenue +42% YoY in Q3, Q3 EPS beat 31%, FY+1 consensus up from 18.6 to 23.0 over 90 days, 1Y +45%, above 50d and 200d. Its 1y daily beta to SPY from Argus history is ~-0.5, so it hedges the tech-heavy core. European winter demand is the near-term driver. Valuation is high vs its own history (P/E 87th pct), so 10% size. Exit on a close below the 200d (~261) or if FY+1 estimates start falling.",
    "review_on": "2027-02-25",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.286333+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.286337+00:00"
   },
   {
    "id": 5,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "XLV",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Sector tilt to health care, the strongest sector in Argus's heatmap: 1M +11.3%, 3M +12.2%, YTD +22%, above 50d and 200d, low beta (~0.3 vs SPY over 1y, vol 17%). Defensive while rates are 5%+ and tech is breaking down (XLK 1M -13%). Exit if XLV closes below its 50d and the sector drops out of the top three on 1M.",
    "review_on": "2027-01-15",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-16T02:16:08.304583+00:00",
