   },
   {
    "id": 6,
    "account_id": 1,
    "symbol": "TMUS",
    "kind": "thesis",
    "text": "Defensive value in an Extreme-fear tape (F&G 11.8, S&P -1.9% on 11-16, XLK -3.2%; breadth shows new highs in staples/health care). P/E ttm 16.4 = 5th percentile of its own 5y range in Argus, forward ~11.9, FCF $18.7B ttm (~10% FCF yield), dividend 2.4%, revenue +7-11% YoY for 3 quarters, op margin ~24% in Q2/Q3, Q3 EPS beat +8%. FY+1 EPS consensus up 13.90->14.01 over 90d; analysts 24 buy / 4 hold, mean target 225. 1y daily beta to SPY ~-0.34 (Argus history), Finnhub 0.38: diversifies the tech/META exposure. Down 21% 1Y and below its 200d (~186) but back above its 50d (~164). Risk: leverage (liabilities/equity 1.6), price war with peers. Size ~9%. Exit on a close below 150 (near the 52w low 143.75 area) or if revenue growth drops under 5% at the late-Jan report.",
    "review_on": "2027-01-29",
    "archived": false,
    "created_by": "ui",
    "created_at": "2026-11-17T02:17:36.554324+00:00",
